    a: "It establishes an explicit, documented baseline that everyone agreed to at a specific point in time — which is what makes change control possible afterward (you can only detect and manage 'change' relative to an agreed starting point) and gives the delivery team confidence to build against a stable target instead of a moving one. Skipping it doesn't eliminate disagreement, it just defers the disagreement to a much more expensive point — after something's already built.",
