    cat: "Analysis",
    lvl: "med",
    q: "Write the main success scenario (numbered steps) for a use case: 'Customer returns a purchased item at checkout.'",
    sol: "1. Customer presents item and receipt to Staff. 2. Staff scans item and retrieves original transaction. 3. System confirms the item and transaction are eligible for return (within return window, item condition acceptable). 4. Staff confirms refund method with Customer. 5. System processes refund to the confirmed method. 6. System updates inventory to reflect the returned item. 7. Staff provides Customer a return receipt. Postcondition: transaction recorded as returned, inventory updated, refund issued.",
    exp: "The main success scenario stays on the happy path only — 'item not eligible for return' or 'refund fails' belong in separate alternate/exception flows, not woven into this sequence.",
