    q: "Apply functional decomposition to the vague business function 'handle customer returns' down to at least 2 levels.",
    sol: "Level 1 (sub-functions of 'Handle Customer Returns'): Validate Return Eligibility, Process Refund, Update Inventory, Notify Customer. Level 2 (decomposing 'Validate Return Eligibility'): Check Return Window, Check Item Condition, Check Original Purchase Record, Determine Applicable Return Policy Exceptions. Each level-2 item is now concrete enough to elicit specific business rules and requirements against.",
    exp: "Decomposition stops once a sub-function is specific enough to attach concrete, testable requirements to — going further than necessary just adds documentation overhead.",
