    sol: "1) Before migrating, ensure the existing Excel RTM has complete ID/source/status data for all 150 requirements — clean up any gaps now, since migration will be much harder once data is split across two systems. 2) Map the Excel structure to the target structure (which Excel columns become JIRA fields vs Confluence content) before moving anything, so the mapping is deliberate rather than improvised row-by-row. 3) Migrate in batches by business capability/epic rather than all 150 at once, validating each batch's traceability (source → JIRA item → test case) before moving to the next, so errors are caught early and don't compound across the full set. 4) Keep the original Excel file as a read-only historical reference (not actively maintained) rather than deleting it, in case a migration error surfaces later and the original data is needed to reconstruct something. 5) Communicate the cutover date to the whole team clearly so no one keeps updating the old spreadsheet in parallel, which would silently reintroduce exactly the drift the migration was meant to fix.",
